[h2]Hello, [strike]Shoomers[/strike] Shoppers, it's Summer Sale time![/h2]

[b]What was done:[/b]
[list]
[*] KEY REMAPPING FEATURE added to PAUSE -> OPTIONS menu. 
[*] Updated game engine version (Unreal Engine 5) from 5.2 to 5.4 (needed for key mapping feature).
[*] Removed the DLSS Nvidia plugin. Quite strange but this gave FPS boost at a low level of graphics;
[*] More types of enemies spawn loot, "Abomination" (big guy) spawns random 3 loot pieces;
[*] More (all) types of enemies counted into relevant achievement (kill n-enemies to unlock);
[*] ChainSaw makes blood splat/squash additional sound at damage;
[*] Fixed bug when Rocket-projectile cause 1 HP damage;
[*] Increased Plasma gun damage;
[*] Improved lights in E1M0, changed pickups, enemies, small tweaks etc.;
[*] Other minor changes;
[/list]

But there are a few side effects from the game version update:
1: build size increased from 600 to 680 MB;
2: from prev. step:  UE 5.4 currently contains bug with direction light: [url=https://forums.unrealengine.com/t/stationary-directional-light-not-working-in-5-4/1890207/2]here[/url] and [url=https://forums.unrealengine.com/t/ue5-4-and-5-4-1-shadows-are-broken-in-vr-vr-template-default-settings/1841528/11]here[/url]. This causes absence of shadows from ceiling/walls inside some parts of levels. 
Since it's quite a priority bug, I assume it will be fixed soon by Epic Games in the next version of UE.

Have a nice end of the week.
Cheers.
--
Serhii.

[h2]Hello, Booters and Shooters!
[/h2]
I spent a good chunk of this weekend working on game improvements.

[b]What was done: 
[/b]
[list]
[*] Text outline in all UI (menus, dialogues, etc.);
[*] Text block centered in dialogues;
[*] Vending machine (shop) spawn items of the same type with small coordinates deviations (increase readability);
[*] Player footstep rate reduction (from ~200 to ~300 units means sound will be triggered 1.5 times less than before);
[*] Fixed bug when footstep sound played when players were riding lift/platform;
[*] Sprint logic changed: one time 'Shift' press - now enabling 'Auto-Sprint' or vice versa;
[*] Added Voiceover slider sound volume to options - so players could get rid of protagonist one-liners completely;
[*] Added mouse sensitivity slider (in the range 0.5-2.5 where 1.0 is Unreal Engine default sensitivity);
[*] Fixed bug when "Quicksave" / "Quickload" could be used only once;
[*] Added "Portal VFX" and sound for the point where the player placed the "Quicksave" portal;
[*] Improved all levels of lighting.
[*] Added sound FXs to "Console of Mudrota" dialogues;
[*] Other minor changes;
[/list]

That's it for now.
--
Cheers
Serhii.

[h3]Hello, Shoomers![/h3]

As my virtual accountable partners - you will receive weekly status updates (as well as a new build for the demo version of 'Shoomer Booter').

So today on our menu:

[list]
[*] Finished assignment of some enemies to spawn pickups at the rest of  'Episode 1' levels;
[*] E1M5 - fixed 'Level Finished' HUD bug;
[*] Tweaked 'Secret areas' at the level 'E1M6';
[*] Added placed 'names' or pickups (weapon, ammo, health) on crosshair over;
[*] Finished assignment of 'hero phrases' after enemy ambushes at the rest of the 'Ep. 1' levels;
[*] Added death fall sound for 'Abomination' enemy;
[*] Fixed bug when 'pause menu' buttons were clickable from the 'options menu';
[*] Added 'shop'/'vending machine' entity (HUD, logic, model, etc.);
[*] Added 'shop' to demo level, tweaked demo level layout to fit 'shop';
[*] Added new pickups: 'Armor Orb', 'Health Orb';
[*] Added 'Quick Save' & 'Quick Load' functionality (logic, HUD messages, Mapping HUD mention, etc.);
[*] Some tweaks at majority of levels (lighting, meshes, enemies, pickups, etc);
[/list]

Feel free to share your playing experience!

--

Cheers,
Tommy Gun Walrus
